02:04:38,211 --> 02:04:42,594
And until that happens, I don't really think we're having a conversation about whether it will be in the budget.

1151
02:04:44,055 --> 02:04:46,057
That's just my opinion based on

1152
02:04:46,813 --> 02:04:53,657
the vote of seven members who in affirmative said we will no longer charge for food.

1153
02:04:54,237 --> 02:04:54,477
Right.

1154
02:04:54,637 --> 02:05:05,403
But I think, and I appreciate that, but we're not charging for lunch right now based on the federal regulations and on the committee's directive, right?

1155
02:05:06,764 --> 02:05:08,165
We haven't charged anyone for lunch.

1156
02:05:08,745 --> 02:05:15,629
What I'm saying is that if you don't want us to charge anyone for lunch next year, we're going to need to

1157
02:05:16,672 --> 02:05:27,519
factor that into the budget, because there is going to be a cost associated with that, unless, as I think we all hope, the legislature takes that out of our hands.

1158
02:05:28,159 --> 02:05:44,650
At the moment, where the reason that I would be inclined to recommend that the directive be suspended, at least for the upcoming school year, is that I can't even tell you what that cost would be, because there's really no way of making a projection

1159
02:05:45,238 --> 02:05:50,679
with respect to participation, which is what would, in part, determine the financial implication.

1160
02:05:51,039 --> 02:06:04,523
So I think it is necessary to talk about in the budget, because if the committee feels as though we should continue to move forward with the mandate, then we're going to have to take a guess on the financial implication.

1161
02:06:05,623 --> 02:06:09,544
It may cause a significant number of other disruptions.

1162
02:06:10,284 --> 02:06:15,005
And I can't tell you exactly what those are, because I can't tell you exactly what the financial implication of it is.

1163
02:06:15,478 --> 02:06:19,499
So that is why it's coming up in the context of the budget.

1164
02:06:21,720 --> 02:06:22,800
Thank you, Mr. Murphy.

1165
02:06:22,840 --> 02:06:24,101
Thank you, Mr. Russo.

1166
02:06:24,121 --> 02:06:29,342
And if I just may speak on that issue, I too want everybody to have free lunch.

1167
02:06:29,422 --> 02:06:34,944
And I pray that the state comes through for us because it could be upwards of a million and a half dollars.

1168
02:06:35,004 --> 02:06:38,085
So I just want to make sure that that's clear.

1169
02:06:38,145 --> 02:06:43,827
And if it's between children that can afford it paying and teachers or

1170
02:06:45,580 --> 02:06:50,263
Professionals not having a job, we just, we have to weigh those options as we move forward.

1171
02:06:51,184 --> 02:06:56,927
Member Hayes.

1172
02:06:57,668 --> 02:07:05,333
I thought, my understanding was that it was currently in the budget, the state budget to fund lunches through next year.

1173
02:07:07,264 --> 02:07:09,304
I don't know if anyone else has more information on that.

1174
02:07:09,324 --> 02:07:15,526
I thought, I thought that was kind of a done deal already, but it just, the budget isn't a done deal.

1175
02:07:15,566 --> 02:07:19,327
So yes, my understanding is that there's support at the legislature.

1176
02:07:19,347 --> 02:07:25,428
I don't, I'm hopeful, but this is something that would have a significant impact on our district.

1177
02:07:25,448 --> 02:07:36,991
So it's sort of one of those ones that we can't really rely on them because if we plan for it, if we plan to implement this directive and

1178
02:07:38,463 --> 02:07:41,846
you know, we don't have a potential cost associated with it.

1179
02:07:42,346 --> 02:07:57,899
And the legislature, for whatever reason, does not, if it doesn't make it into the final version of the budget, the state budget, we could have created a significant problem for ourselves locally, which is again, why I think we have a responsibility to discuss it here.

1180
02:08:03,023 --> 02:08:05,325
May I, Mayor?

1181
02:08:05,385 --> 02:08:06,426
Yes, Member McLaughlin.

1182
02:08:07,237 --> 02:08:12,799
And, but we won't know that right until July one, whether it's, it's been passed in the governor's budget.

1183
02:08:13,639 --> 02:08:14,019
Correct.

1184
02:08:14,400 --> 02:08:16,980
I mean, presumably, yes.

1185
02:08:17,041 --> 02:08:20,042
I mean, there's been times where I don't think it'll be before July one.

1186
02:08:20,102 --> 02:08:23,443
And there are times where certain provisions have ample support.

1187
02:08:23,463 --> 02:08:35,387
So you can start to rely on it in times when, you know, there are continuing resolutions of some kind and it goes further into the summer, but that sort of, I think more that sort of

1188
02:08:36,148 --> 02:08:40,312
reaffirms the point that there's a lot of uncertainty associated with this.

1189
02:08:44,295 --> 02:08:44,675
Mayor?

1190
02:08:45,736 --> 02:08:50,100
Member Graham, Member Russo.

1191
02:08:51,761 --> 02:08:58,287
If I recall back, maybe even like before the pandemic, when we were talking about

1192
02:09:00,847 --> 02:09:01,988
Um, a pilot.

1193
02:09:02,048 --> 02:09:08,310
We did a pilot way back when and a big central part of that was like tracking participation.

1194
02:09:08,330 --> 02:09:19,014
Um, to help inform like whether we would qualify for some program or or another, um, After that, and it was this like predated Mr Murphy for sure.

1195
02:09:19,034 --> 02:09:20,254
Um Are.

1196
02:09:22,035 --> 02:09:25,096
I think I heard you say you can't size this.

1197
02:09:25,236 --> 02:09:29,198
Does that is that because we're not tracking or because we lack data?

1198
02:09:30,752 --> 02:09:32,933
from the city in the revolving account?

1199
02:09:32,973 --> 02:09:34,933
Like, why can't we size this?

1200
02:09:35,433 --> 02:09:36,734
We can track participation.

1201
02:09:36,754 --> 02:09:43,575
The concern is that with all of lunch being free this year, that participation could be at one number.

1202
02:09:44,116 --> 02:09:47,697
And if we were to charge, the participation would be another number.

1203
02:09:48,317 --> 02:09:59,220
Or if it's free in a second year, I mean, all of those variables could have an impact on what the potential reimbursement would be.

1204
02:10:01,505 --> 02:10:05,606
And so that, again, if the committee wants us to attempt to do this, we can.

1205
02:10:05,666 --> 02:10:11,288
But what would happen is we will have to come back with a number, with a projection.

1206
02:10:11,308 --> 02:10:19,510
I will be inclined to be conservative with that projection because of the potential domino effect that would occur if we miss.

1207
02:10:20,411 --> 02:10:25,512
And then we can put it to the committee for consideration.

1208
02:10:29,898 --> 02:10:31,980
there's a significant amount of risk involved with this.

1209
02:10:33,361 --> 02:10:51,173
Last year, the food services budget finished with an operating deficit of over a half million dollars, which we were able to pull back to some degree with some funding that we received subsequent based on appropriations related to specifically for food services in different school districts.

1210
02:10:51,273 --> 02:10:55,536
But the deficit was significant.

1211
02:10:55,896 --> 02:10:57,337
We expect to surplus this year

1212
02:10:58,001 --> 02:11:05,405
Um, but again, to the point you just raised, we don't have, we don't have those numbers, um, to the penny at the moment.

1213
02:11:07,506 --> 02:11:20,952
And, um, I think also before your time led by the mayor, the entire city signed a hunger free pledge and advocates from the

1214
02:11:22,488 --> 02:11:42,283
task force, I don't know exactly like the right term to use for the people actually trying to make sure that we politicians keep good to our commitment to make Medford hunger free have reached out and asked us asked several of us about, you know, what, you know,

1215
02:11:44,050 --> 02:11:47,531
what Medford Public Schools, you know, how Medford Public Schools fits into all of this.

1216
02:11:49,412 --> 02:11:59,536
And what I have relayed to them is that I don't think there's anyone on the committee who is not interested in proceeding as we have stated in our policy.

1217
02:11:59,716 --> 02:12:00,096
However,

1218
02:12:02,597 --> 02:12:10,240
you know, that is all contingent on funding that comes from the mayor and the city in terms of how we spend.

1219
02:12:10,621 --> 02:12:26,748
And in lean times, we start to have to pit things like feeding kids lunch against administrators and that that's like never a good situation to be in because everybody loses when the community has to have that

1220
02:12:27,909 --> 02:12:36,093
kind of debate about money as it relates to basic necessity and needs.

1221
02:12:36,173 --> 02:12:51,199
So I say all that to say there are people who probably are or may not be on this call who are watching at the city level to make sure that the city keeps good on its promises that were unanimous.

1222
02:12:53,400 --> 02:12:55,341
And Mayor, I don't know if they've reached out to you.

1223
02:12:55,561 --> 02:12:57,142
I know there's

1224
02:12:57,677 --> 02:13:04,738
or it sounds like there is actual activity happening on that task force that the school committee has not been made aware of, which I think is great.

1225
02:13:04,879 --> 02:13:11,280
I also think the school committee needs to like be looped in somehow in a formal way, which I think was the intent.

1226
02:13:12,260 --> 02:13:25,163
But overall, I think as we proceed, I think we do need to at least understand what it would cost to do this thing that we've all promised to do really rather excitedly and unanimously.

1227
02:13:27,660 --> 02:13:30,041
at multiple times actually over the last couple of years.

1228
02:13:30,101 --> 02:13:40,504
So I also think based on what I am hearing that the outlook is good and favorable from a statewide perspective.

1229
02:13:40,604 --> 02:13:53,869
So I am of the mind that like, I want us to be ready with an understanding of the impact in case that goes South, but that I'm actually not overly worried that it will go South.

1230
02:13:53,989 --> 02:13:56,710
I just want us to be prepared to be able to decide

1231
02:13:58,146 --> 02:14:02,266
what the implications are for us if it does.

1232
02:14:03,449 --> 02:14:08,471
But I know that's a lot of work and a bunch of information you may or may not have.

1233
02:14:08,531 --> 02:14:10,992
So I don't know how best to proceed with that.

1234
02:14:11,212 --> 02:14:13,493
Just to be clear, it's more the latter than the amount of work.

1235
02:14:13,513 --> 02:14:15,814
The amount of the work, I think, is Ms.

1236
02:14:15,854 --> 02:14:18,055
Graham's point where the committee feels unanimously about this.

1237
02:14:18,075 --> 02:14:22,157
There's no one in the school administration that really wants to charge students for lunch either.

1238
02:14:22,197 --> 02:14:27,699
I think, again, the philosophical underpinnings of this are something that we all agree with.

1239
02:14:27,779 --> 02:14:33,101
And we've talked in the past about not wanting to have a public school system that's

1240
02:14:33,857 --> 02:14:37,580
littered with with user generated fees to fund it.

1241
02:14:37,620 --> 02:14:41,103
So I think there's unanimity of use on the preference here.

1242
02:14:41,923 --> 02:14:55,533
But from a practical perspective, and I think just using the point that Miss Graham makes about the city, you know, when we make a budget request that's based on a number of FTEs, we can multiply those FTEs by this year 70,000.

1243
02:14:56,134 --> 02:15:00,357
And if it turns out that some of the personnel we retain for those FTEs

1244
02:15:00,830 --> 02:15:12,836
costs a little bit more or a little bit less based on the experience of the individuals coming in, there's a certain level of, again, art, not science, to those projections.

1245
02:15:12,896 --> 02:15:19,800
And we can feel as though we're doing right by the committee and right by the community, as long as we're able to stay within that reasonable range.

1246
02:15:20,400 --> 02:15:29,945
In a situation like this, in which we frankly, we can come up with a number, but I have a responsibility to tell the committee that it's not really based in anything

1247
02:15:31,113 --> 02:15:46,861
particularly factual, and I have concerns that the number could turn out to be way off, then either the city could appropriate significant more funding that is necessary to advance this particular priority, or it could appropriate funding that could be very much short of that priority.

1248
02:15:47,262 --> 02:15:59,328
And in that world, when we're advocating before the municipal government, the mayor and the council, I am hesitant to just not be able to recommendation that as a school administration, we can stand behind

1249
02:16:00,099 --> 02:16:06,144
with a certain degree of confidence, and that's why I feel the need to flag this particular initiative.

1250
02:16:07,746 --> 02:16:13,371
Yeah, and I understand and appreciate that.

1251
02:16:14,111 --> 02:16:25,942
I do think the other thing this committee needs perhaps more education on, whether from the Food Security Task Force or somebody else, is

1252
02:16:27,385 --> 02:16:35,853
The value of providing free lunch has less to do with feeding a kid whose parents may be able to afford it.

1253
02:16:35,873 --> 02:16:37,635
It is not about that at all.

1254
02:16:38,436 --> 02:16:45,943
It is about opening up access to the kids who desperately need to be able to eat lunch at school.

1255
02:16:46,735 --> 02:16:57,883
For for a whole variety of reasons, who may or may not qualify under the states program whose parents may or may not want to qualify them under the free lunch programs and.

1256
02:16:59,464 --> 02:17:01,766
When it becomes a normalized part of the process.

1257
02:17:02,977 --> 02:17:03,758
everybody wins.

1258
02:17:04,178 --> 02:17:14,024
And when every kid in school isn't hungry, every kid in school benefits from all the kids in school being able to focus on learning and not worrying about being hungry.

1259
02:17:14,104 --> 02:17:17,566
And I'm like far from the expert in the room on this topic.

1260
02:17:17,746 --> 02:17:19,967
I know there are people who feel way more passionately than I do.

1261
02:17:19,988 --> 02:17:31,695
I think my suggestion for the superintendent and I can follow up with you in an email is that we find somebody from the food security task force to engage with us to make sure we're all on the same page about

1262
02:17:33,195 --> 02:17:41,001
this program and how it fits into the master plan for the excited declaration that we made about being hunger free here in Medford.

1263
02:17:46,404 --> 02:17:49,907
We can definitely follow up with that and provide that information.

1264
02:17:49,947 --> 02:18:00,754
I just I just I think I wanted from the outset as I did last month, just flag this as something that while there are some things that if if

1265
02:18:01,872 --> 02:18:04,894
If our request is fulfilled, we know what we can do and how.

1266
02:18:05,355 --> 02:18:07,476
In this case, I don't even know what the request would be.

1267
02:18:07,516 --> 02:18:09,197
So that's just something we'll have to work on.

1268
02:18:09,217 --> 02:18:11,559
Thank you.

1269
02:18:11,579 --> 02:18:12,200
Member Rousseau?

1270
02:18:15,722 --> 02:18:16,263
Thank you, Mayor.

1271
02:18:17,063 --> 02:18:19,485
I just want to call out a couple of things.

1272
02:18:19,665 --> 02:18:26,810
First of all, I understand that there is literally no one, probably no one even in the entire Zoom here, who wants to charge kids for food.

1273
02:18:28,612 --> 02:18:29,432
Maybe I'm wrong, but

1274
02:18:30,975 --> 02:18:38,162
You know, the drop in participation is absolutely will happen.

1275
02:18:38,522 --> 02:18:45,448
As we know this last year, participation was very robust over previous normal years.

1276
02:18:47,070 --> 02:18:50,012
And, you know, the effects of the pandemic are not done.

1277
02:18:50,192 --> 02:18:51,914
There are lots of people who are still hurting.

1278
02:18:52,675 --> 02:18:55,858
And as Member Graham mentioned, there are lots of people for which applying

1279
02:18:58,214 --> 02:19:01,296
represents in their minds a security risk to their families.

1280
02:19:01,797 --> 02:19:05,359
And it's not really an appropriate decision that anybody should have to make.

1281
02:19:05,759 --> 02:19:08,421
And I don't think anybody here is saying that's okay either.

1282
02:19:09,882 --> 02:19:12,704
I do have a question about whether or not ESSER funds could be used for this.

1283
02:19:12,724 --> 02:19:17,308
I think that there's an argument that they could.

1284
02:19:17,328 --> 02:19:27,295
And I think that's one of the, I mean, that might be something we have to look at, but this is one with an unknown price tag.

1285
02:19:27,974 --> 02:19:34,500
And depending on what that price tag is, it could have a disproportionate impact on the availability of the ESSER funding.

1286
02:19:35,060 --> 02:19:39,504
Not in a way that I think somehow this could blow through, you know, multi-million dollars.

1287
02:19:39,524 --> 02:19:41,265
I don't think that would happen.

1288
02:19:42,847 --> 02:19:51,153
But what could happen is that essentially we pump this issue down the road a year or two.

1289
02:19:51,954 --> 02:19:54,917
And then as the ESSER funding is expiring, particularly if the

1290
02:19:55,821 --> 02:20:06,069
and the appetite of the Legislature has diminished for this then we could just move this problem further down the road.

1291
02:20:06,910 --> 02:20:17,358
And I would say just sort of like thinking about this from a political science perspective, if every district were to do that, the incentive for the Legislature to do something about it would probably be diminished as well.

1292
02:20:19,179 --> 02:20:24,944
And so I don't, again, I do think that, again, I don't want to

1293
02:20:26,194 --> 02:20:34,461
interpret the ESSER eligibility in a way that is so liberal that it diminishes some of the other ways in which we're interpreting it.

1294
02:20:35,943 --> 02:20:46,272
But my sort of gut reaction having reviewed ESSER 2 and ESSER 3 guidelines is yes, I do think we could probably construe them to include this.

1295
02:20:46,712 --> 02:20:51,256
I just don't know if that would necessarily be a strategic or prudent thing to do.

1296
02:20:54,004 --> 02:20:54,884
Thank you.

1297
02:20:54,904 --> 02:20:58,185
I have been in contact with the Medford Food Security Task Force.

1298
02:20:58,805 --> 02:21:10,288
They were reaching out about how we can, on the school committee, continue to move us towards the Hunger-Free Medford Proclamation that was made.

1299
02:21:11,188 --> 02:21:16,949
And I had indicated that it is the current policy of the school committee that this will continue.

1300
02:21:18,629 --> 02:21:20,430
I didn't answer that as a school committee

1301
02:21:22,083 --> 02:21:25,685
as our opinion, but in fact, it was already voted so on.

1302
02:21:26,466 --> 02:21:46,517
And, you know, I think that the proclamation to make Medford hunger free is, is, well, the city council made it, I don't actually remember if the mayor's office at the time was a participant in that, but, you know, it's, it's three years old, two years old, the proclamation, three years old, I think.

1303
02:21:46,797 --> 02:21:46,917
And,

1304
02:21:48,679 --> 02:21:53,683
you know, that's not a lot of time to be deciding we're just gonna give up on proclamations that we made a big deal about.

1305
02:21:53,883 --> 02:22:02,869
So not having this funded and free is moving us further away from making Medford hunger free.

1306
02:22:02,909 --> 02:22:05,030
I think that should be universally understood.

1307
02:22:05,191 --> 02:22:15,718
So if one direction is that there's nobody hungry in Medford, and one is that there are more people hungry in Medford, not including this in the budget will mean we have decided

1308
02:22:17,848 --> 02:22:26,656
not the administrators, this is not a moral conversation about your desires and intent, but we will have decided to make Medford more hungry.

1309
02:22:28,237 --> 02:22:31,040
It's just a simple fact, can't be denied.

1310
02:22:31,200 --> 02:22:32,081
So thank you.

1311
02:22:34,343 --> 02:22:35,544
We'll report back on this.

1312
02:22:35,804 --> 02:22:38,787
I think the committee has heard our concerns.

1313
02:22:39,427 --> 02:22:40,268
We'll try to

1314
02:22:42,351 --> 02:22:45,372
address this with as much specificity as we can.

1315
02:22:45,452 --> 02:22:57,914
Just understand that I do think there's a little, there's a degree of speculation here that I'm not comfortable with that may turn out to be unavoidable, but we'll present you with that information in the coming weeks.

1316
02:23:00,935 --> 02:23:10,157
Okay, I think we're ready for the final two slides that sort of sum up where we've landed with regard to these priorities.

1317
02:23:10,217 --> 02:23:10,697
And I guess

1318
02:23:11,348 --> 02:23:24,798
As Dr. Cushing prepares slide 16 for us, I will say that just like the categories can potentially shift based on feedback from the committee and even some of the comments that were made tonight were very helpful, we appreciate them.

1319
02:23:26,259 --> 02:23:38,848
As other funding sources are identified, or as we frankly just deliberate upon some of these priorities, between now and the time that the school committee adopts the budget,

1320
02:23:39,678 --> 02:23:45,542
We'll continue to communicate that clearly and make sure that the committee is aware of some of those fluctuations.

1321
02:23:45,922 --> 02:24:01,373
You remember last year that their committee requested one number than the municipal government maybe appropriation, and there was a $760,000 Delta that needed to be bridged and so we identified some of the pieces, and I think it might have been the math coaches last year.

1322
02:24:01,826 --> 02:24:09,531
that we sort of had as a priority that had been listed throughout, but we had said that that might be something that there could be some wiggle room on.

1323
02:24:09,771 --> 02:24:14,254
Frankly, that's another one this year that there could be some wiggle room on.

1324
02:24:14,454 --> 02:24:23,339
And so the $71.4 million number represented, and another caveat that I always mention, and I will again, these are all approximations.

1325
02:24:23,499 --> 02:24:28,022
So when you finally, when you get your budget book, if where we land is $71.4 million,

1326
02:24:29,605 --> 02:24:35,448
it'll be $71 million, $430,000, and a few other numbers and some change.

1327
02:24:35,488 --> 02:24:48,073
But for purposes of this discussion, if we were to incorporate category A only into the operating budget, we would be looking at a $71.4 million request.

1328
02:24:48,713 --> 02:24:52,215
And the way we reach that number moving left to right is the 67.4.

1329
02:24:52,315 --> 02:24:53,135
That includes the 2% in FY

1330
02:24:58,307 --> 02:25:06,534
22 that has not yet been implemented and is still being negotiated, but has been identified throughout our budgeting process going back to last spring.

1331
02:25:06,554 --> 02:25:11,178
Then there's the fixed costs that bring us up to 69.9 million.

1332
02:25:11,218 --> 02:25:17,343
That's the $2.5 million costs in contractual wage increases that are due in FY 23.

1333
02:25:18,224 --> 02:25:23,509
That's your special education tuition and specialized transportation costs.

1334
02:25:24,009 --> 02:25:25,130
And then a few other variable

1335
02:25:25,740 --> 02:25:28,802
fixed cost increases that we're projecting in the hundreds of thousands.

1336
02:25:30,122 --> 02:25:37,686
If we were to incorporate a 2% FY23 cost of living adjustment, that would bring that number up to 71 million.

1337
02:25:38,387 --> 02:25:43,609
If we were to incorporate all of the category A and category B, that number would rise to 72 million.

1338
02:25:43,929 --> 02:25:52,354
